# magic-agent — deployment environment template
#
# Copy to /opt/midas/.env on the VPS (the run/serve systemd units point EnvironmentFile here):
#   cp deploy/.env.example /opt/midas/.env
# The LIVE unit (deploy/midas-agent.service) instead reads /etc/midas/agent.env — see
# deploy/README.md. NEVER commit .env. Placeholders only — fill with real values on the VPS.
#
# FORMAT: this file is consumed VERBATIM by systemd's `EnvironmentFile=`, which does NOT
# strip inline comments and treats everything after `=` as the value. So use plain
# `KEY=value` lines — NO `export`, NO quotes, and NO trailing `# note` after a value.
# Every comment lives on its OWN `#` line. (This also makes it safe to
# `set -a; . .env; set +a` in a shell.)
#
# Run-loop tuning (executor mode, live-data flags, log path) is set via `magic-agent run`
# CLI FLAGS in the systemd unit, NOT here — this file holds secrets/credentials only.

# ── LIVE secrets (REQUIRED for `--executor twak`) ──
# build_app(mode="twak") fails closed BEFORE constructing any live port unless ALL six
# of these are present and non-empty (app.py `_require_live_env` / `_LIVE_REQUIRED_ENV`).
# TWAK is the SOLE signer for BSC swaps and CMC x402 payments. Paper mode needs NONE of them.
TWAK_ACCESS_ID=your-twak-access-id-placeholder
TWAK_HMAC_SECRET=your-twak-hmac-secret-placeholder
TWAK_WALLET_PASSWORD=your-twak-wallet-password-placeholder
# BSC mainnet JSON-RPC endpoint (receipt polling, confirmation depth, balance reads).
BSC_RPC_URL=https://bsc-dataseed.binance.org
# CoinMarketCap API key — REQUIRED in live (the live universe cannot be fetched without
# it; --live-cmc fails closed when absent). Rank/momentum only — CMC NEVER creates setups.
CMC_API_KEY=your-cmc-api-key-placeholder
# The TWAK wallet address (used for balance reads, RPC, and quote provider).
WALLET_ADDRESS=0xYourWalletAddressPlaceholder

# ── Dashboard / API ──
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE: browser-facing base URL the Next.js web app calls for /api/*
# (served by `magic-agent serve` behind the reverse proxy), e.g. https://your-domain.example.com/api
# BUILD-TIME: this is inlined into the web bundle at `npm run build` — set it BEFORE building
# the dashboard, and rebuild after any change (see deploy/README.md Step 4).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=
